@andyzhangx I think there can be many reasons why the controller-manager is restarted during running detach or attach operations e. g. the hosting machine turn into error state, if you run the controller-manager in k8s -> vertical pod autoscaling,... etc.

I understand you can't guarantee that attach/detach works when the controller-manager is restarted, but I don't understand why the controller-manager can't recover the situation autonomously after a restart. 

After restart it tries to attach the volume of the rescheduled pod and this does not work because the volume is still attached to another machine. This is indicated by a `ConflictingUserInput` error from the arm and the controller-manager could react to it properly, right?
